# Wavetable and HDL vector images must keep LF line endings: the documented
# SHA-256 values (docs/evidence/*) and the generator output in
# tools/s6_reference.py are computed on the LF payload.  Without this rule a
# core.autocrlf=true checkout rewrites the tables to CRLF and the recorded
# hashes no longer match the files on disk.
*.hex text eol=lf
# Review archives are checksum-recorded deliverables: their bytes must survive
# a clone untouched, otherwise the recorded SHA-256 values (computed on the
# CRLF working copy) no longer describe the checked-out files.  This rule must
# stay last so it wins over the *.hex rule above for paths under archive/.
archive/** -text